            cancer
  JOURNAL   Cancer Res 60 (8), 2140-2145 (2000)
   PUBMED   10786676
COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AF211943.1.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            On Nov 22, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_016373.3.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a member of the short-chain
            dehydrogenases/reductases (SDR) protein family. This gene spans the
            FRA16D common chromosomal fragile site and appears to function as a
            tumor suppressor gene. Expression of the encoded protein is able to
            induce apoptosis, while defects in this gene are associated with
            multiple types of cancer. Disruption of this gene is also
            associated with autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia 12.
            Disruption of a similar gene in mouse results in impaired
            steroidogenesis, additionally suggesting a metabolic function for
            the protein. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript
            variants. [provided by RefSeq, May 2014].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (1) represents the longest
            transcript and encodes the longest isoform (1).
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
